UID:fa-39776@ev3nts.filmakademie.de
DTSTAMP:20261006T015716Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20261001T133000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20261001T141500
SUMMARY:Alumni Case Study: Woodblock - Going Spherical and Beyond
LOCATION:Caligari
DESCRIPTION:Pflicht\nDozent*innen: Ilija Brunck\n\nCo-founder Ilija Brunck 
 traces Woodblock's path from its Filmakademie roots to recent large-scale 
 productions at Sphere Las Vegas\, and shares what's next for the studio.\n
 \nhttps://ev3nts.filmakademie.de/user/student/?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-
 01
CATEGORIES:Pflicht
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fa-39777@ev3nts.filmakademie.de
DTSTAMP:20261006T015716Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20261001T143000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20261001T151500
SUMMARY:Alumni Case Study: Same Craft\, Different Business
LOCATION:Caligari
DESCRIPTION:Pflicht\nDozent*innen: Julian Weiss\n\nA degree in VFX or anima
 tion looks like a ticket to one specific industry. It isn't. It is trainin
 g in judgement - knowing what makes an image hold\, what makes a story lan
 d\, how a production actually gets finished.\n\nJulian Weiss looks back br
 iefly at the pivots that took him from VFX supervision to an agency for in
 teractive formats\, then forward at the part that matters more: navigating
  change and building on AI.\n\nhttps://ev3nts.filmakademie.de/user/student
 /?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-01
CATEGORIES:Pflicht
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
